M4.1 — Protocol State store wired into production (SSE cursor journal)
========================================================================
Node: M4.1 (Protocol State store)
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 2 exit work (between-nights M4 program)
Revision: commit "M4.1: protocol-state journal wired as the daemon's SSE
replay-cursor store" on main
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: LOGIC-ONLY — the crate's durable JSONL
journal with prefix-consistent replay and torn-tail tolerance had unit
tests and ZERO production callers; SSE clients had to remember their own
offsets and a reconnect after a Core restart replayed from zero)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- Daemon::bind_with_protocol_state: the daemon holds a
  ProtocolStateStore (modbit-core opens it at <db-dir>/protocol-
  state.jsonl next to core.db).
- GET /events?client=<id> WITHOUT an explicit since resumes from the
  client's last PERSISTED cursor (latest-wins per consumer id — new
  ProtocolStateStore::last_cursor). Cursors persist durably
  (append+flush) per advanced batch; journal append failure is
  fail-open for the live stream (replay semantics are at-least-once by
  construction). bind() (persistence off) preserved for existing
  callers.

